<item><title>CON26/29 Blake Street Carpark Redevelopment - Registration of Interest</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> This Registration of Interest is the first stage of procurement for the redevelopment and expansion of the Blake Street Public Carpark in Rangiora Township.<br /><br />The works will include:<br /><br />- Stripping, relevelling, and resurfacing of the bulk carpark area.<br /><br />- Replacement of approximately 130m of AC watermain with new DN150-DN200<br /><br />- Removal of existing kerbs, gardens, and lighting assets<br /><br />- Construct new kerbs, channels, and additional underground drainage to tie into the existing network<br /><br />- High amenity paving areas with street furniture <br /><br />- Adjusting the existing lighting network including installing and commissioning new poles and luminaires, and extending the cable and duct network<br /><br />- New carpark linemarking and signage<br /><br />- Construction of new garden areas and tree pits ready for planting (by others)<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Waimakariri District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 02/Sep/2026 04:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2655<br /><b>Contact person</b> : CJ Schuyt Email: chris.schuyt@wmk.govt.nz Tel: +64 3 266 9031<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/tsi.axd?id=42e8da21ac8d44ef85ceae5b1c801a57s2655s85818252ab0f4a97ad4749bb758701e4s12</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">42e8da21ac8d44ef85ceae5b1c801a57</guid>
<pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 03:21:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
</item>
<item><title>Rangiora Eastern Link - Physical Works - Registration of Interest</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Rangiora Eastern Link (REL) is a proposed 3 km new collector road designed to relieve traffic congestion on Southbrook Road, enhance transport efficiency, and unlock new residential areas in East Rangiora and commercial development in Southbrook. The expected cost estimate for the project is $65.9 million including physical and enabling works, fees and land acquisition.<br /><br />Council has approved the Business Case and co-funding has been confirmed for the pre-implementation phase from NZTA. Following review of the responses to a recent Market Sounding (Contract reference 26/16) , this invitation is to register interest to be shortlisted and invited to tender for the physical works contract as well as provide services during the design phase (ECI).<br /><br />Council is seeking experienced civil contractors with the capability and capacity to construct the Rangiora Eastern Link. Approximately three contractors will be shortlisted and initially engaged under separate fixed-fee Early Contractor Involvem...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Waimakariri District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 09/Sep/2026 04:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2654<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Products & Materials, Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=069a38cffa7c478f971bdbb05b207f38s2654</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">069a38cffa7c478f971bdbb05b207f38</guid>
<pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 09:26:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Building Products &amp; Materials</category>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
</item>
<item><title>Asbestos Property Survey and reinspection</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Waimakariri District Council is seeking registrations of interest from suitably qualified and experienced asbestos surveying consultancies to support the next stage of its district-wide asbestos management programme. <br /><br />The opportunity covers a diverse portfolio of Council-owned buildings and structures and is expected to include surveys of previously unsurveyed pre-2000 assets, reinspections of known asbestos-containing materials, confirmatory sampling, and correction of existing survey and register information where required. The final delivery approach may comprise a combination of targeted reinspections and full management surveys, with priority given to unsurveyed properties and locations containing higher-risk materials.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Waimakariri District Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 02/Sep/2026 04:00 pm (UTC+12:00) Auckland, Wellington time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP2645<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Engineer, Research, Tech services, Real Estate & Property Services, Waste Management & Landfill<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 2]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.nz/PublicTenderAccess.aspx?id=0da8583ec5004e939c9c21522c211df8s2645</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">0da8583ec5004e939c9c21522c211df8</guid>
<pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 20:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Engineer, Research, Tech services</category>
<category>Real Estate &amp; Property Services</category>
<category>Waste Management &amp; Landfill</category>
</item>
